  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#6c9429020c6cc80b4581ce4dc17318ec59f0998a08af3bdc11803627ce8a297e</id>
    <title>Useful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-28T00:33:11Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-1" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">When a new neighbour arrives, a brief introduction plus one specific offer—such as collecting a parcel—makes it easier for them to accept help without guessing what’s available.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#50dec1db46defa0b04d93a76ab55c312ce42de5c6c4dfb28b3942587f79c4f51</id>
    <title>Hopeful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-28T00:33:11Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-2" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">During the 1940s, Britain’s wartime allotments turned spare ground into food-growing plots; neighbours shared tools and know-how, showing how overlooked patches can become productive together.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#e5d4539366a01e87914ca329605a0ce3e85a817a5b393f614819a06b67d69adb</id>
    <title>Action</title>
    <updated>2026-11-28T00:33:11Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-3" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At home, check one frequently used drawer for a small snag—such as a loose handle or tangled cables—and spend three minutes tightening or untangling what you can by hand.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
